ot a suggestion — it's a hard limit. A user in Sydney requesting a file from a server in Virginia waits roughly 200 milliseconds just for the round trip, before your server does a single useful thing. No amount of code optimization fixes physics. A CDN (Content Delivery Network) fixes it the only way physics allows: by moving the content closer to the user. Netflix, YouTube, and every fast website you've ever used lean on this trick.", "start": 15.05, "end": 41.125, "words": [{"text": "The", "start": 15.3, "end": 15.375}, {"text": "speed", "start": 15.375, "end": 15.638}, {"text": "of", "start": 15.638, "end": 15.725}, {"text": "light", "start": 15.725, "end": 15.988}, {"text": "is", "start": 15.988, "end": 16.1}, {"text": "not", "start": 16.1, "end": 16.288}, {"text": "a", "start": 16.288, "end": 16.35}, {"text": "suggestion", "start": 16.35, "end": 16.975}, {"text": "it's", "start": 16.975, "end": 17.213}, {"text": "a", "start": 17.213, "end": 17.275}, {"text": "hard", "start": 17.275, "end": 17.575}, {"text": "limit", "start": 17.575, "end": 18.35}, {"text": "A", "start": 18.35, "end": 18.575}, {"text": "user", "start": 18.575, "end": 18.875}, {"text": "in", "start": 18.875, "end": 19.025}, {"text": "Sydney", "start": 19.025, "end": 19.325}, {"text": "requesting", "start": 19.325, "end": 19.788}, {"text": "a", "start": 19.788, "end": 19.85}, {"text": "file", "start": 19.85, "end": 20.175}, {"text": "from", "start": 20.175, "end": 20.312}, {"text": "a", "start": 20.312, "end": 20.375}, {"text": "server", "start": 20.375, "end": 20.712}, {"text": "in", "start": 20.712, "end": 20.788}, {"text": "Virginia", "start": 20.788, "end": 21.2}, {"text": "waits", "start": 21.2, "end": 21.488}, {"text": "roughly", "start": 21.488, "end": 21.788}, {"text": "200", "start": 21.788, "end": 22.263}, {"text": "milliseconds", "start": 22.263, "end": 22.8}, {"text": "just", "start": 22.8, "end": 22.988}, {"text": "for", "start": 22.988, "end": 23.087}, {"text": "the", "start": 23.087